WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.150
It's so lovely to see you again.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.853
After that ferocious
feline chased you off,

00:00:11.853 --> 00:00:14.946
I never thought you'd leave
your country cottage.

00:00:14.946 --> 00:00:17.646
&gt;&gt; Hm, yes, I don't much care for
the city, but

00:00:17.646 --> 00:00:21.200
I really needed to buy
some Stilton cheese.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.710
&gt;&gt; The country mouse is on the something,
cities allow for

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.890
large markets that provides specialized
products, like gourmet cheese.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.610
&gt;&gt; You can't buy fancy cheese, or
much else that's good in the country.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:37.329
&gt;&gt; No, no, I've got Amazon Prime,
I can order almost anything else online.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.730
&gt;&gt; Amazon Prime is a great
example of how transportation and

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.640
logistics can deliver a wide range of
products across America and the world.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:51.394
&gt;&gt; You can't sample cheeses when shopping
online, and there aren't great specialized

00:00:51.394 --> 00:00:55.200
services, like whisker waxing
salons out in the country.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.650
&gt;&gt; But when I order online,
I can avoid the crowds.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.990
I hate lines and I hate traffic.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:05.770
&gt;&gt; The average commute time for
a New York City resident is 40 minutes.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:09.100
The average commute time in
Montana is just 18 minutes.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.490
&gt;&gt; I just listen to music
when I'm stuck waiting.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.910
&gt;&gt; Well I have a short commute and
I can hear the crickets at night.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:22.440
&gt;&gt; True, you don't have to deal with
traffic, but jobs pay more in the city.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.800
&gt;&gt; On average, wages go up by about 5%
as metropolitan area density doubles.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.830
&gt;&gt; Sure, you make good money,
but what about housing?

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.810
I'd never pay such sky high rent.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.273
&gt;&gt; Housing prices also typically go
up by about 5% as metropolitan area

00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:38.970
density doubles.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:46.080
&gt;&gt; Yes, but I have the best museums,
shows, and restaurants.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.600
&gt;&gt; This cafe is very nice.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.950
&gt;&gt; City dwellers basically share the fixed
costs of supporting a variety of cultural

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.110
institutions.

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.720
Urban density also
increases the bump rate,

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.720
the chance of meeting someone new and
exciting.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.970
&gt;&gt; But cities are dangerous.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:07.160
&gt;&gt; I always feel safe in the city,
there are so many eyes on the street.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.620
&gt;&gt; Crime is an unfortunate
reality in American cities, but

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.330
most have become a lot
safer since the 1980s.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.100
In fact, New York City has a lower
murder rate than the country as a whole.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.970
&gt;&gt; And really the best thing about
cities is the endless novelty.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:27.270
The new opportunities, the new ideas,
the new rodents, it's all so exciting!

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.780
&gt;&gt; Give me my warm, safe cottage any day!

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.921
&gt;&gt; Okay, but while you're visiting,
wanna catch a show?

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.473
You know, Cats is playing!

00:02:37.473 --> 00:02:47.473
[MUSIC]

